{{Quote|Commander, the additional reinforcements have arrived.''"<br />"''Tighten your grip, K2-B4. The Republic will almost certainly attempt a second mission to infiltrate our defenses and rescue the prisoners. I'm counting on you to ensure that nothing slips past our blockade.|K2-B4 and Osi Sobeck, regarding the fleet|<ref name="Citadel Rescue" />}}
A '''fleet''' of various [[Starship|ships]] served in the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]]' [[Confederacy of Independent Systems Navy|naval forces]] during the [[Clone Wars]] in formation of a [[blockade]] in [[orbit]] of the [[planet]] [[Lola Sayu]]. The fleet consisted of one [[Providence-class Dreadnought|''Providence''-class Dreadnought]], one [[Lucrehulk-class battleship|''Lucrehulk''-class Battleship]],<ref name="The Citadel" /> and four [[Munificent-class star frigate|''Munificent''-class star frigates]], which also carried [[Vulture-class starfighter|Vulture droid starfighters]], [[Hyena-class Droid Fighter/Bomber|''Hyena''-class Droid Bombers]], and [[droid tri-fighter]]s.<ref name="Citadel Rescue" />

In [[20 BBY]],<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' places the [[mission to Mortis]] and the [[Battle of Mon Cala]] to [[20 BBY]]. As the episode this event takes place within takes place between the events of the episodes the other events are attached to according to {{SW|url=news/star-wars-the-clone-wars-chronological-episodeorder|text=''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' Chronological Episode Order}}, this event must also take place 20 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|BBY]].</ref> a [[Shuttle 81572|stolen]] [[Sheathipede-class Type B shuttle|''Sheathipede''-class Type B shuttle]] carrying a [[Galactic Republic]] rescue team crossed paths with the fleet before landing on Lola Sayu, where they were to [[Battle of Lola Sayu|retrieve]] [[Jedi Master]] [[Even Piell]], who had been [[Capture of Even Piell|imprisoned]] in the [[Citadel]].<ref name="The Citadel" /> Later, the defense fleet, under the command of the [[T-series military strategic analysis and tactics droid|T-series tactical droid]] [[K2-B4]], came into a brief engagement with a Republic [[Lola Sayu task force|task force]], which had been sent to retrieve the rescue team and the coordinates of the [[Nexus Route]], a [[hyperspace route]] that spanned to the hearts of both Republic and Separatist [[homeworld]]s.<ref name="Citadel Rescue" />

{{Military-stub}}

